91:Precondition resources are automatically injected into agent prompts by `task-board spawn`. Full prompts preserve normal text inlining. Lite prompts use the resolved `agent_context.prompt.preconditions` policy: by default, text below `inline_bytes` is rendered inline, while larger text and binary resources are written read-only under `.temp/resources/` and represented by their name, description, byte count, SHA-256 digest, and local path. This means:
93:1. Attach instructions/specs as precondition resources to a task
95:3. Agent saves results via `task-board m 'add_resource(..., type=outcome)'` on first write, then `update_resource(...)` for revisions
102:- **Use explicit create/update/delete** — `add_resource` / `resource add` must not silently overwrite; use `update_resource` / `resource update` when replacing an existing payload
103:- **Use adopt only for local repair** — `resource adopt` registers bytes already stored at `.resources/<elementID>/<relative-resource-path>` without rewriting them; a missing payload returns resource-not-found and an existing declaration returns resource-exists
105:- **Use safe relative resource paths** — `/` separates validated path segments; empty, dot/traversal, absolute/drive-qualified, backslash, control-character, malformed escape, and encoded/repeatedly encoded separator or traversal forms are rejected in local and remote storage
106:- **Attach files, not folders** — directories only organize resource files and never satisfy resource existence or handoff evidence
107:- **Always use board commands** — never create/edit resource files or progress.md resource sections manually
108:- **Name handoff evidence with task scope** — keep the task ID in the resource path, for example `reports/TASK-260218-abc_architecture-design.md`, so `task-board handoff` can recognize it
